Subject: [PATCH 4/5] server: replace detached stream workers with nonblocking
 I/O

Move upstream TCP I/O into the existing network thread and remove
per-stream workers and pipes. Give sockets, stream contexts, and write
queues a single owner, unlinking PicoQUIC's borrowed pointers before
destroying streams.

Handle asynchronous connects, partial writes, bounded buffering, and
directional half-closes without blocking the packet loop. Use actual
recv results rather than stale errno or peeked lengths.

Fix connection-close use-after-free and cleanup paths, prevent aborted
streams from recreating upstream connections, and reap abandoned
connections using PicoQUIC's handshake and idle deadlines.
