From 0d0ddca01b259bd7bb9ee4e5d77f1555f54abf55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Artem S. Tashkinov" <birdie-github@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 19:58:23 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] server: preserve reads after disconnected TCP half-close

Treat ENOTCONN from shutdown(SHUT_WR) as a completed write half-close
once queued writes have drained. Keep the receive direction available
to drain buffered responses or EOF instead of resetting the QUIC stream.

Add stream IDs, descriptor numbers, byte counters, queued-byte counts,
and FIN state to upstream connect, send, recv, and shutdown diagnostics.
